---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Terms of Use · Datawake"
  description="Terms of use for the Datawake browser extension and website."
>

<Nav />

<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>These terms cover your use of the Datawake browser extension and the datawake.app website.</p>
    <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:16px;">Last updated: 3 October 2026</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container policy-content">

  <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
  <p>
    By installing the Datawake extension or visiting datawake.app, you agree to these terms.
    If you do not agree, please do not use Datawake.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Datawake is</h2>
  <p>
    Datawake is a browser extension that shows which companies track you on the websites you visit. If you
    leave those settings on, it clicks "Reject" on cookie banners for you and sends the Global Privacy
    Control signal. If you turn on fingerprint protection, it adds invisible noise to what scripts can read
    about your device. It does not block trackers or change the content of websites.
  </p>
  <p>
    Datawake can draft letters to companies and complaints to data protection authorities from what it
    recorded. These are drafts for you to read and send yourself. Datawake is not a law firm and nothing it
    shows you is legal advice. Whether a site broke the law is for the authorities and courts to decide.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Free plan</h2>
  <p>
    The free version of Datawake is available to everyone with no payment required. We reserve the right
    to change the features included in the free plan with reasonable notice, but we will not remove core
    tracker detection features without providing a paid alternative or retiring the product.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Datawake Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Datawake Pro is not available yet. Before it launches, we will add its terms here, including pricing,
    how to cancel and your right of withdrawal, and nothing will be charged until you choose to subscribe.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>You may use Datawake for personal, lawful purposes. You may not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use Datawake to infringe on the privacy of others</li>
    <li>Reverse engineer, modify, or redistribute Datawake in violation of the open-source licence</li>
    <li>Use Datawake in any automated or scripted way that places unreasonable load on third-party services</li>
    <li>Misrepresent Datawake or claim affiliation with us</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Open source licence</h2>
  <p>
    The Datawake extension source code is available under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0). The licence terms are in the
    GitHub repository. You are free to fork, study, and modify the code under those terms.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data and privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our data practices are covered by our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. The short version:
    your browsing data never leaves your device, and we do not collect or store it.
  </p>

  <h2>8. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Datawake is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind. We aim to keep it working well, but we
    cannot guarantee that tracker data is always complete or up to date. The internet changes fast.
    Some trackers will be missed, and some identifications may be imperfect.
  </p>
  <p>
    We are not responsible for decisions you make based on the information Datawake shows you.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, Datawake's liability for any claim arising from these terms is
    limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim arose. We are not liable for
    indirect or consequential damages.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of Spain. Disputes will be resolved in the courts of Barcelona,
    unless you are a consumer in the EU, in which case you may also bring proceedings in the country
    where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. For material changes, we will give at least 14 days' notice via email
    (Pro subscribers) or a notice on the website. Continued use after notice means you accept the
    updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:hello@datawake.app">hello@datawake.app</a>.
  </p>

</div>

<Footer />

</Base>
